## Conversation
User wanted their PR branch auto-rebased: poll every 30s, rebase when behind, then run gpo.sh -f. Started as an inline snippet, then a temp script, then this permanent script. Requirements evolved to: detect the default branch (not assume main), work from git worktrees while keeping the local default branch in the main checkout updated, prefer the upstream remote over origin, rebase without opening an editor, and on conflicts fail plus send a macOS notification. Later swapped the INTERVAL env var for a -i flag and split the startup info onto separate lines.

## Actions
Created local-bin/auto-rebase.sh. Validated with shellfmt.sh (shellcheck + shfmt clean). Committed with git commit -s -S using a commitlint-validated message.

## Errors & Mistakes
First draft used a zsh shebang; shellcheck does not support zsh (SC1071), so it switched to bash. The Claude Code sandbox blocked chmod/commit in this repo until the user disabled it; commitlint's cache install also needed XDG_CACHE_HOME redirected to a temp dir under the sandbox.

