## Hints for Future Agents
The user's grbm alias is `git rebase -S -i`; the script keeps -S -i but sets GIT_SEQUENCE_EDITOR=true to auto-accept the todo list (GIT_EDITOR alone is not enough for interactive rebase). Default branch is read from `git ls-remote --symref <remote> HEAD`, not local origin/HEAD, which can be stale or unset. `git rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-common-dir` locates the main checkout from any worktree; a fetch from a worktree updates shared remote-tracking refs, so the rebase target is fresh even when the main checkout is on another branch. Unattended `git rebase -S` stalls if the signing key needs a passphrase or touch.

